From 0313192625e58eec5cc43d5a44f489c24468756d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefane Fermigier <sf@abilian.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:18:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 142/142] OdfFile reader: deleted text in a deleted frame is
 well-formed

Text deleted inside a frame that is itself in a deletion was written as
<w:del> into whatever run was open, then the run closed before </w:del>:
<w:r><w:del><w:delText>..</w:delText></w:r></w:del>, which is not XML,
and the writer lost every tracked change after it on the way back. The
unique change ids of fix/odt-changed-region-unique-id exposed it: before, duplicate ids made
the reader write the first region's text for every piece, so the frame
was never reached, and its text silently replaced. The open run is now
closed before the deletion starts its own.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 OdfFile/Reader/Format/paragraph_elements.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/OdfFile/Reader/Format/paragraph_elements.cpp b/OdfFile/Reader/Format/paragraph_elements.cpp
index adeea8a995..865b7dad49 100644
--- a/OdfFile/Reader/Format/paragraph_elements.cpp
+++ b/OdfFile/Reader/Format/paragraph_elements.cpp
@@ -209,6 +209,8 @@ void text::docx_convert(oox::docx_conversion_context & Context)
 		if (state.type == 2)
 		{
 			add_del_run = true;
+			// A run may be open: the deletion wraps a run of its own, or the tags cross
+			Context.finish_run();
 			Context.output_stream() << L"<w:del>";
 		}
 	}  
